"""Derive SkyyWardrobe/build_skyywardrobe_0.2.5.py from the SET pin 0.2.4 (build_skyywardrobe_0.2.4.py, GENERATED by
tools/wardrobe_0_2_4_patch.py; 0.2.4 stays untouched) AND SkyyWardrobe/test_skyywardrobe_0.2.5.py from test_skyywardrobe_0.2.4.py.
Edit THIS file, never the generated scripts: python tools/wardrobe_0_2_5_patch.py, then python SkyyWardrobe/build_skyywardrobe_0.2.5.py
(never --deploy from an agent). Test: python SkyyWardrobe/test_skyywardrobe_0.2.5.py

0.2.5 = THE POOL LIST SCROLLS + TAKE OUT STAYS OUT.
  1. SCROLL (Skyy 2026-10-16, on the Requip page's pool list ARMOR / WEAPONS / ITEMS / INVENTORY with 8 rows and '< Page 1 / 2 >':
     "allow scrolling here." + the standing ask of the day: scroll lists instead of pages). The pool area #SkyyRqPa becomes the kit's
     scroll_list (TopScrolling, vanilla scrollbar, on the list well - the same container the LOADOUTS list already uses), the same height as
     before (8 rows show at once). Every view draws its WHOLE list in it: Armor / Weapons / Items rows and the pet / ability / modifier
     pickers up to ROW_MAX rows (150, the SkyySacks packet-size cap), the Magic Bag blocks grid up to GRID_MAX cells (17 rows of 9), Your
     inventory = both old pages in one grid (hotbar + storage, then worn armor + backpack: 10 rows). Over the cap = the list line says
     "The first 150 of N - search to find the rest". The '<' / 'Page n / m' / '>' buttons go; their row keeps Sort (same place) + a count
     line (#SkyyRqPg). Row size, element ids (#SkyyRqP<n>, the click "pc" + index into cells[] = the eid the row showed), sort, search,
     the selected-entry detail panel and Pick it / Take out / Forget are unchanged; rows are narrower by the well padding + scrollbar
     (RW). The LOADOUTS list already scrolls (scroll_list since 0.2.0, 18 loadouts at most) - unchanged.
  2. TAKE OUT STAYS OUT (Skyy 2026-10-16: "make it so, if you click take out, the auto store doesn't put it back in automatically."):
     Take out (op 8) of a gear item now marks THAT item with the metadata key SkyyRequipOut = { p: "<profile key>" } (nothing personal).
     Auto-store skips an item marked for the profile it runs for - across relogs, restarts and SkyyGear metadata changes (0.2.4's
     session-only kind count WdAuto.KEEP missed those; it is kept as a second guard). A hand deposit (clicking it on the page, Deposit all
     gear, /requip dump, the bridge deposits, an Equip that stores it) clears the mark: WdCodec.stamp() drops it, so a pool entry never
     carries it; WdCodec.unstamp() drops it too, so every "same item?" check (the crash repair's countKindU evidence, census, kinds)
     sees a marked item exactly as the plain one - the mark is ON the one item, never a record, so it can never make an item exist twice.
     Another profile's mark (traded / dropped) is ignored. The mark stays on the item if it leaves and comes back (it was taken out by hand).
Classes changed: WdCodec (OUTK, markOut, outOf; stamp / unstamp bodies), WdTx (depAllSkip body), WdOps (op 8 body), WdPage (layout +
build + pc bound). No saved-file change, no command, no config row, no bridge key. ROLLBACK to 0.2.4: nothing is lost; 0.2.4 ignores the
mark (its old session rule applies) and its stamp() keeps the key on a pool entry, harmless (dropped by 0.2.5's next stamp / unstamp).
"""
